<title>HONG KONG: HK July orders on hand fall 7 pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK July orders on hand fall 7 pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said July orders-on-hand fell seven percent in value terms on the year against a six percent drop in June.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders-on-hand in July 1996 over July 1995 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						  July 1996   June 1996</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey    -7	   -6</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				 -3	   -4*</p>
<p> Textiles					  -8	   -9</p>
<p> Electronic Products			   -15	  -7</p>
<p> Electrical products			   -5	   -9</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		   +23	  +25</p>
<p> Plastic products				-14	  -13</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		     +8	   -14</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
